        "bookmarked": false,
        "raw": "<p>Hello everybody.</p><p>Now, I know that when using an attack that hits multiple targets, any tokens (like aim and attack+1) only apply to one target. My question is, how exactly does that work? For example, if I Use 3 attack+1 tokens and an aim token, and use Bunker&#39;s Grenade Launcher and it hits 2 people, one of those people is getting hit with 4 dice and the other is getting hit with 7 with all the die getting converted to the highest (after removing auto misses of course). So if I want to resolve the aimed, higher dice pool attack first( I am assuming that since it is my turn I can choose wich target gets hit first?) how does that seccond one work? Do I just re-roll 4 dice for the seccond target or do I have to keep track of what die was what and wich ones were the token dice and all that?</p><p>Not sure if I missed something that explains this better or not. It game up in a game last night and we just had the guy re-roll 4 dice because it seemed&nbsp; much easier, but then I thought I read somewhere that the same dice roll was used for all targets of an aoe attack. Any clarification anyone could bring would be awesome.</p><p>Thanks.</p>",
